---
code: cli-unknown-flag-did-you-mean
when-fires: an unrecognized flag that IS within edit-distance 2 of a real one. cli/lib.rs parse_args_from. {flag} is the token, {suggestion} the nearest real flag.
why: AID-NEEDS:law-codes-vary-by-world-not-grammar: the sibling of cli-unknown-flag, split by a WORLD-STATE (the flag table has a near neighbour) with its own remediation.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc plan --boook --book=webhost.sh
dorc: error[cli-unknown-flag-did-you-mean]: Dorc does not recognize the flag
`--boook`; did you mean `--book`?
usage: dorc [probe|plan|apply] --book=<book.sh> [--pre-source <sh>]... [--debug-argv]

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: cli-unknown-flag-did-you-mean
{{flag}} = "--boook"
{{suggestion}} = "--book"
